      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "reasoning": "Verified in the files. ahmed mvi-architecture/SKILL.md lines 120-128 collect the effects flow in a plain `LaunchedEffect(Unit) { viewModel.sideEffects.collect { ... } }` with NO repeatOnLifecycle. rcosteira android-dev/SKILL.md line 57 explicitly mandates the opposite: 'Collect it in a `LaunchedEffect` (lifecycle-scoped via `repeatOnLifecycle`), never `collectAsStateWithLifecycle`', and the example at lines 90-99 wraps the collect in `lifecycle.repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED) { viewModel.effects.collect { ... } }`. Both sides use the same source stream — `Channel(Channel.BUFFERED).receiveAsFlow()` (ahmed lines 67-68; rcosteira lines 79-81) — so the only divergence is the collection site, and it is a genuine opposing-pattern conflict. With plain LaunchedEffect the composition stays alive while the Activity is STOPPED, so an effect emitted while backgrounded is consumed immediately (off-screen navigation/snackbar); rcosteira's repeatOnLifecycle cancels collection when STOPPED so the buffered Channel replays on resume. This is the exact behavior rcosteira's rationale depends on, and ahmed's template defeats it. Real conflict on the same decision."
    },
