      "description": "Initial load dispatched from LaunchedEffect(Unit) re-fires on activity/composition recreation, reloading data on every rotation.",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "reasoning": "Verified mvi-architecture lines 131-133: `LaunchedEffect(Unit) { viewModel.onIntent(HomeIntent.LoadItems) }`. On configuration change the Activity/composition is recreated by default, so LaunchedEffect(Unit) enters composition fresh and re-runs, re-dispatching LoadItems. loadItems() (lines 84-96) then sets isLoading=true and re-fetches, replacing state.items on the already-populated (retained) ViewModel — a redundant reload/spinner flash per rotation. A ViewModel `init{}` block (as android-patterns line 107 uses) runs once and survives config change, avoiding this. Real behavior; the defect only manifests on config change and the fetch may be cheap if cached, so 'minor' is the correct severity."
    }
